        {
          "source_quote": "ἔτι μᾶλλον ἰλιγγίων ἐν τοῖς πράγμασιν. διὸ ἐκ τοῦ τῆς ψυχῆς βάθους ἐστέναζον",
          "english_quote": "and reeling still more amid these questions, I therefore groaned from the depth of my soul.",
          "issue": "ἰλιγγίων is a finite first-person imperfect here, not a participle coordinated with ἐπιστήσας. The Greek states increased dizziness as the result of his realization, then introduces groaning with διό. The draft retains the experience but subordinates that assertion to the groaning, flattening the sequence. This is a translation issue, not evidence of defective print.",
          "suggested_revision": "End the sentence beginning “Having at last realized” with “I was reeling still more amid these questions.” Then begin the next sentence: “Therefore I groaned from the depth of my soul.” Preserve the intervening content. The revised wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
